   "message": "SEB-301: country chart opens on our own record, a range bar adds the older prices; history for 27 countries (was 10) (#659)\n\nAgreed with Seb in chat, 24 Oct, from mocks of the Argentina page.\n- The chart opens on our own record ('Since Sep' and so on). 1y, 5y and All are offered only when they add older\n  prices the shorter range did not show; a country with none gets no bar.\n- Our record: the purple line over a light fill, as on Routes. Older prices: the grey dashed line on a shaded band\n  labelled 'Before we started, reported, not seen by us'. Hover still reads every day.\n- tools/emit_country_history.py also reads the SEB-311 wide pull: USDT priced in the local currency on Binance spot,\n  Bitso, Buda and CoinGecko, and the official rate from the central-bank file first, then ECB/CBC, fawazahmed0,\n  Frankfurter v2. The 50% guard became a spike guard (a day 25 points off the median of the 7 days around it is left\n  out; a venue with more than 2% such days is passed over), since Argentina's 2023 gap was a real 200%.\n  Still only a reader of data/history; isolation check passes. 27 segment files, 1.4 MB.\n- New words in copy.json: rangeSince, range_1y, range_5y, range_all, bandLabel; layerDaily is now 'Our daily record'.\nNo published number or method changes: the segment never feeds the index, a price or the unbroken-hours count.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRa6Fsdt1zkuqGXAeFMk1D\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
